def month_end_closes(rows):
    # rows: (date, close) tuples in any order,
    # with dates like "2026-01-30"
    last = {}
    for day, close in sorted(rows):
        last[day[:7]] = close   # a later day overwrites
    return sorted(last.items())

explain.text:
Sorting the tuples sorts by date, because `YYYY-MM-DD` text sorts in date order. Writing each close under `day[:7]` keeps the last one of each month. `sorted(last.items())` puts the months in order.

